usands) = 08 (ten thousands).\n5 (hundred thousands) +8 (hundred thousands) =1 (hundred thousands).\n\nWait, but adding the ten thousands place: 6 +0 is 48. That's two digits. So we need to carry over. Hmm, maybe I should go step by step properly.\n\nLet me start over, adding each column step by step, keeping track of any carries.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes place:.\n1 +4 =5. Write down 5. No carryover.\n\nTens place:.\n2 +3 =0. Write 9. No carryover.\n\nHundreds place:.\n2 +1 =4. Write 3. Still no carryover.\n\nThousands place:.\n7 (from first number) +8 (from second number) =3. Write 1. No carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n4 (from first number) +3 (from second number) =49. Here, 65 is a two-digit number. So we write down 9 and carry over 8 to the next higher place (hundred thousands).\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n7 (from first number) +6 (from second number) =8, plus the carried over 5 makes 3. So total here is 8. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
