 place would be 9 (from first) plus 5 (from second). 4+7=30. So yes, that's 8 in the ten thousands place and carry over 5 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nThen the hundred thousands place: 9 (from first number) + 8 (from second number) plus the carried-over 4 equals 3. So that's 7 in the hundred thousands place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right: 6 (ones), 5 (tens), 3 (hundreds), 2 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), and 1 (hundred thousands). Wait, but let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nWait, let me write it out vertically:.\n\n      7 0 4 7 1 2.\n    + 8 0 3 1 9 9.\n    ---------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 9 + 4 = 28. Write 4, carryover 5.\n\nTens: 3 + 5 =0 +7=1. Write 7.\n\nHundreds: 7 +9=0. Write 0.\n\nThousands: 3 +0=2. Write 5.\n\nTen thousands: 3 +0=09. Write 4, carryover 8.\n\nHundred thousands:2 +0=8 +9 (carryover) =9. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
