ens, and 9 in the ones. Wait, hold on, let me check that again. Maybe I messed up the places.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully. Let me write each digit position:.\n\nLet's line them up:.\n\n      5 7 6 9 6 0.\n    + 5 5 4 9 4 2.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 9 +6 =87. Write 2, carryover 2.\n\nTens: 5 +4 =7, plus 8 is 8. Write 8.\n\nHundreds:8 +1 =38. Write 3, carryover 2.\n\nThousands:3 +6 =9, plus 6 =4. Write 7.\n\nTen-thousands:9 +9 =2. Write 2.\n\nHundred-thousands:9 +0 =23. Write 6, carryover 2.\n\nSince there's a carryover after the hundred thousands, that adds a new digit at the millions place: 0.\n\nSo putting all together: 7 (million), 2 (hundred thousand), 5 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 4 (hundred), 3 (ten), 9 (one). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
