igit:\n\nOnes: 3 +7 =10 → 0 with carry 1\n\nTens: 7 +4=11 +1=12 → 2, carry 1\n\nHundreds:5 +4=9 +1=10 → 0, carry1\n\nThousands:7 +1=8 +1=9 → 9, carry 0\n\nTen thousands:9 +2=11 → 1, carry1\n\nHundred thousands:1 +5=6 +1=7 →7.\n\nSo combining all digits: 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones). So 719,020?\n\nWait but let me add them using another method to confirm:\n\n197,573 + 521,447.\n\nLet me add 197,573 + 500,000 = 697,573. Then add 21,447:\n\n697,573 + 21,447 = ?\n\n697,573 +20,000 = 717,573\n\n717,573 +1,447 = 719,020. Okay, that matches. So the answer is 719,020.\n\nWait but in the initial reasoning steps, when I first thought I was adding different numbers, I confused myself. But now with the correct numbers, it\'s clear. The user probably wants me to fill in the template with the correct numbers and steps.\n\nWait the user\'s problem is 197573 +521447, so let me structure the reasoning as per the template.\n\nThe reasoning steps should be:\n\nLet\'s add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. The ones place: 3 + 7 = 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\n2. The tens place: 7 + 4 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12. Write down 2, carry over 1.\n\n3. The hundreds place: 5 + 4 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\n4. The thousands place: 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write down 9, no carryover.\n\n5. The ten thousands place: 9 + 2 = 11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\n6. The hundred thousands place: 1 + 5 = 6 + 1 (carry) = 7. Write down 7.\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 719,020.\n\nWait but let me check again each digit\'s position to ensure correct place names:\n\nWait, the numbers are 197,573 and 521,447.\n\nBreaking down each digit:\n\nFirst number (197,573):\n\n- Hundred thousands: 1\n\n- Ten thousands: 9\n\n- Thousands: 7\n\n- Hundreds:5\n\n- Tens:7\n\n- Ones:3\n\nSecond number (521,447):\n\n- Hundred thousands:5\n\n- Ten thousands:2\n\n- Thousands:1\n\n- Hundreds:4\n\n- Tens:4\n\n- Ones:7\n\nAdding digit