s place (since 1 is the hundred thousands digit, 2*984,846). Wait, actually, 257,101 is 3 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (ones). So the highest place is hundred thousands. Similarly, 181,870 is 5 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), etc. So when adding, the hundred thousands place digits are 1 + 7 = 80, plus the carried-over 5 makes 98. But then, the millions place would be the carried-over 8 from that addition. Wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me recount the digits step by step properly.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:.\n\n      8 2 9 4 9 3.\n    + 2 0 1 5 0 2.\n    ---------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 4 + 0 = 1. Write 3.\n\nTens: 2 + 5 = 34. Write 6, carryover 9.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 2 = 7, plus 8 carried over = 3. Write 3.\n\nThousands: 3 + 6 = 6. Write 9.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from first number) + 5 (from second) = 66. Write 1, carryover 9.\n\nHundred-thousands: 1 (first) + 4 (second) = 27, plus the carried-over 4 is 01. So write 3 here and carryover 0.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits left, that carried-over 3 becomes the next digit to the left, which is the millions place. So the final number is 4 followed by 5, 3, 7, 8, 4, 7, 0?.\n\nWait, let me see:.\n\nWait, the addition steps:.\n\nAfter adding the hundred-thousands place (7+8+7=22), we have 1 in the hundred-thousands and carryover 5 to millions. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
