 thousands place:2\n\n- Ten thousands place:7\n\n- Thousands place:5\n\n- Hundreds place:5\n\n- Tens place:1\n\n- Ones place:4\n\nNow adding each column:\n\nOnes:1 +4 =5 → digit:5\n\nTens:1 +1 =2 → digit:2\n\nHundreds:8 +5 =13 → digit:3, carryover 1\n\nThousands:2 +5 =7 +1 (carryover) =8 → digit:8, no carryover?\n\nWait 2 (from first) +5 (second) =7, plus the carryover 1 → 8. So no new carryover.\n\nTen thousands:7 (first) +7 (second) =14 → digit 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 (first) +2 (second) =7 plus carryover 1 → 8.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:2\n\nOnes:5\n\nSo the number is 848,325. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 848,325. I need to present this in the template provided.\n"]  6%|6         | 32/500 [39:46<9:59:06, 76.81s/it]
