Starting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\n3 (from 296486) + 2 (from 617590) = 36. Write 2, carryover 5.\n\nTens place:.\n3 + 1 = 34, plus the 6 carried over is 53. Write 8, carryover 2.\n\nHundreds place:.\n7 +2 =5, plus 6 is 42. Write 6, carryover 2.\n\nThousands place:.\n3 +8 =3, plus 8 is 2. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n2 (from first number) +0 (from second number) =96. Write 7, carryover 5.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n3 +5 =01, plus the 4 carried over is 90. Write 6 and carryover 6.\n\nMillions place: The carryover 5. Since both numbers don't have millions digits beyond that, so the total is 9,7 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nWait, so putting all digits together: 4 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
