nTens place:7 +5 =12. Write 2. Carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:0 (first number's hundreds) +8 (second's hundreds)=8, plus carryover 1 makes 9. Write 9. Carryover 0.\n\nThousands place: first number's thousands digit is 0, second's is5. So 0+5=5. No carryover. So thousands digit is 5.\n\nTen thousands place: first number has 5 (ten thousands), second has 0. So 5 +0=5.\n\nHundred thousands place: first has4, second has2. 4+2=6.\n\nPutting all together:\n\nHundred thousands:6, ten thousands:5, thousands:5, hundreds:9, tens:2, ones:4. So the number is 655,924.\n\nWait but let me confirm with actual addition:\n\n450,573\n\n+205,851\n\n= ?\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\n450,573 + 200,000 = 650,573\n\nThen add 5,851: 650,573 +5,851 = 656,424?\n\nWait, that's conflicting with previous. Hmm, so there must be a mistake in my digit-by-digit approach.\n\nWait let's do it again step by step:\n\nWrite down the numbers vertically:\n\n\u2003450573\n\n+205851\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3 +1 =4 \u2192 4\n\nTens:7 +5 =12 \u2192 write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:0 +8 =8 +1(carry)=9 \u21929, no carryover.\n\nThousands:0 (from first number) +5 (from second) =5. No carryover. So 5.\n\nTen thousands:5 (from first) +0 (from second) =5.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +2=6.\n\nSo the total would be 655,924.\n\nBut adding the numbers directly:\n\n450,573 +205,851:\n\n450,573 +200,000 =650,573\n\n650,573 +5,851:\n\n650,573 +5,000 =655,573\n\n655,573 +851 = 656,424. Wait, so there's a discrepancy here. That means my digit-by-digit approach must be wrong.\n\nWait where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, let's do digit by digit again carefully:\n\nNumbers:\n\nFirst number: 450573\n\nDigits from right:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):3\n\nPosition 2 (tens):7\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):5\n\nPosition4 (thousands):0\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):5\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4\n\nSecond number:205851\n\nDigits from right:\n\nPosition1:1\n\nPosition2:5\n\nPosition3:8\n\nPosition4:5\n\nPosition5:0\n\nPosition