digit, the sum might be a seven-digit number here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, actually, let me go through each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nAligning the numbers:.\n\n```.\n  516541.\n+ 604576.\n----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 1 = 5 ✔️.\n\nTens: 6 + 5 = 8 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 9 = 3 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 9 + 0 = 0 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands: 1 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 93. So write 4, carry over 0. ✔️.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 + 2 = 8, plus the carried 5 makes 83. So yes, that's 21. So the hundred thousands place becomes 5, and we have to carry over 5 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried 7 becomes the new digit in the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
