s would result in writing 0 and carryover 1. So we need to add a new digit at the million place.\n\nSo the total digits are:\n\nMillion place: 1\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:4\n\nThus the total is 1,087,034.\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\n654,383 + 432,651:\n\nLet\'s compute it another way:\n\n654,383 + 400,000 = 1,054,383\n\nThen add 32,651: 1,054,383 +32,651 = 1,087,034. Yes, that matches.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,087,034.\n\nWait, but let me check the digit-by-digit addition again to be sure.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3+1=4 ✔️\n\nTens:8+5=13, so 3 with carryover 1 ✔️\n\nHundreds:3+6=9 +1=10 → 0 carryover 1 ✔️\n\nThousands:4+2=6 +1=7 ✔️\n\nTen thousands:5+3=8 ✔️\n\nHundred thousands:6+4=10 → 0 and carryover 1. So adding the carryover to the next (million) place, resulting in 1,087,034. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 1,087,034. I need to present this in the template provided.\n'] 13%|#3        | 65/500 [1:21:27<9:50:41, 81.47s/it]
