ns.\n\nLet me start over carefully.\n\nFirst number: 981,991\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (ones):\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 1\n\nPosition 2 (tens):9\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):9\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):1\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):8\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):9\n\nSecond number: 367,692\n\nPositions:\n\n1 (ones):2\n\n2 (tens):9\n\n3 (hundreds):6\n\n4 (thousands):7\n\n5 (ten thousands):6\n\n6 (hundred thousands):3\n\nNow adding each digit:\n\n1. Ones place:1 +2=3. No carryover.\n\n2. Tens place:9+9=18 →8, carryover 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:9 (first) +6 (second) +1 (carryover) =16 →6, carryover 1.\n\n4. Thousands place:1 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carryover) =9 →9, carryover 0.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:8 (first) +6 (second) =14 →4, carryover 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:9 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carryover) =13 →3, carryover 1.\n\n7. Millions place: carryover 1 →1.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nMillions place:1\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:3\n\nThus the total is 1,349,683.\n\nAh, that makes sense. So earlier mistake was in the hundreds place digits, I had misread the first number's hundreds digit as 1 instead of 9. So the correct answer is 1,349,683.\n\nLet me verify with another method: 981,991 + 367,692.\n\nAdding 981,991 + 367,692:\n\n981,991 + 300,000 = 1,281,991\n\n1,281,991 +67,692 = ?\n\n1,281,991 +60,000 =1,341,991\n\n1,341,991 +7,692 = 1,349,683. Yes, that matches.\n\nSo the correct sum is 1,349,683. I need to make sure the reasoning steps are correctly written now.\n"] 14%|#3        | 69/500 [1:27:55<10:56:44, 91.43s/it]
