arry over 6 to the millions place. But since there are no more digits, that carried over 5 becomes a 4 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 0.\n\nTens: 7.\n\nHundreds: 3.\n\nThousands: 6 (with a carryover).\n\nTen thousands: 8 (with a carryover).\n\nHundred thousands: 5 (from 96, so the 6 is in the hundred thousands, and the carried over 2 makes a new million digit).\n\nMillions place: 7.\n\nSo combining all those digits: 4 (million), 8 (hundred thousand), 1 (ten thousand), 7 (thousand), 3 (hundred), 7 (ten), 5 (one). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
