nSo when adding:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 7 + 8 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nTens: 8 + 9 = 9. Write 5.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 8. Write 0.\n\nThousands: 6 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 36. Hmm, so here we have 70 in the thousands place. Wait, but thousands place can only have a single digit. So we need to carry over. 72 thousands is 2 ten thousand and 9 thousands. So we write down 6 in the thousands place and carry over 8 to the ten thousands place.\n\nTen thousands place: The first number has 3, the second has 9. Adding the carried over 8: 2 + 2 + 4 = 0. So 3 in the ten thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 + 4 = 8. No carry-over here.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 4.\n\nTens:9.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nThousands:6 (with a carryover of 5 to ten thousands).\n\nTen thousands:9.\n\nHundred thousands:6. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
