s place:1 +3=4\n\nThousands place:1 +8=9\n\nTen thousands place:3 +1=4\n\nHundred thousands place:5 +8=13.\n\nWait, let's do it step by step properly, digit by digit.\n\nFirst, let's break down each number digit-wise:\n\nFirst number: 531,111\n\nDigits from right to left (ones to hundred thousands):\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:1\n\nHundreds:1\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nSecond number:818,308\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nOnes:8\n\nTens:0\n\nHundreds:3\n\nThousands:8\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nNow, adding each column starting from the right:\n\nOnes place:1 +8 =9 → write 9, no carryover.\n\nTens place:1 +0 =1 → write 1, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place:1 +3 =4 → write4, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:1 (from first) +8 (from second) =9 → write9, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:3 (first) +1 (second) =4 → write4, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place:5 (first) +8 (second)=13 → write3 and carryover 1.\n\nSince there are no higher digits, the carryover 1 becomes the next digit (millions place).\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:9\n\nTens:1\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands:9\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nMillions:1\n\nSo the total is 1,349,419.\n\nWait, let's confirm by another method. Let's add the numbers:\n\n531,111 +818,308.\n\nBreak them down:\n\n500,000 + 30,000 +1,000 +100 +10 +1\n\nplus\n\n800,000 +10,000 +8,000 +300 +0 +8.\n\nAdding together:\n\nMillions: 0 +0 =0 (but carryover may occur)\n\nWait, adding each part:\n\n500k +800k =1,300,000\n\n30k +10k=40k → total so far 1,340,000\n\n1k +8k=9k → 1,349,000\n\n100 +300=400 → 1,349,400\n\n10 +0=10 → 1,349,410\n\n1 +8=9 → total 1,349,419. Perfect, matches the previous result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1,349,419.\n\nWait, but let me check again with vertical addition to be absolutely sure.\n\n\u2003\u202f531,111\n\n+818,308\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:1+8=9\n\nTens:1+0=1\n\nHundreds:1+3=