lace and carry over 6 to the millions place. Wait a second, but the original numbers are both six digits, so adding them might result in a seven-digit number. Let me check again.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe I messed up the places. Let me write them out aligned:.\n\n  140,080.\n+ 547,597.\n----------.\n\nBreaking it down digit by digit from right to left (ones to higher places):.\n\nOnes: 0 + 4 = 8 ✔️.\n\nTens: 6 + 6 = 2 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 8 = 1 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 4 + 8 = 58. So write 2, carry over 3. ✔️.\n\nTen-thousands: 4 (from first number) + 4 (from second) + 0 (carry) = 0 ✔️.\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 0 = 29. So here, the hundred-thousands place would be 1, and carry over 5 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, the carried 8 becomes the new millions digit. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
