bers again.\n\nWait, maybe I misread the numbers. Let me confirm:.\n\nFirst number: 397,988. Breaking down the digits:.\n\n- Hundred thousands: 8.\n\n- Ten thousands: 1.\n\n- Thousands: 5.\n\n- Hundreds: 4.\n\n- Tens: 8.\n\n- Ones:0.\n\nSecond number: 611,444:.\n\n- Hundred thousands:3.\n\n- Ten thousands:6.\n\n- Thousands:5.\n\n- Hundreds:1.\n\n- Tens:4.\n\n- Ones:7.\n\nWait, so when adding the hundreds place: the first number's hundreds digit is 9, and the second's is 3. So 4 +4 =36, plus any carryover?.\n\nWait in the hundreds place, the previous step (tens place) had a carryover of 7, so let me retrace:.\n\nWait let's go step by step again:.\n\nOnes place: 7 +4 =60. So 9 written, carryover 3.\n\nTens place: 3 +4 =57, plus carryover 9 is 43. So 9 written, carryover 6.\n\nHundreds place: 0 (from first number) +0 (from second) =04, plus carryover 4 is 54. So here, write 9 and carryover 4.\n\nThousands place: 5 (from first number's thousands place) + 0 (from second's thousands place) =8, plus carryover 8 is 82. So write 7 and carryover 2.\n\nTen thousands place: 3 (first's ten thousands) +2 (second's ten thousands) =29, plus carryover 9 is 63. Write 4, carryover 4.\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 +3 =75, plus carryover 0 is 55. So write 8 and carryover 2.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, that final carryover 8 is added as a new digit at the front.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nOnes:8, Tens:8, Hundreds:2, Thousands:3, Ten thousands:9, Hundred thousands:8, plus the final 6. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
