 down 0 here and carry over 6 to the next higher place.\n\nNow the hundred-thousands place: 5 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) plus the carried-over 2 equals 70. So that's 9 in the hundred-thousands place and a carry-over of 7 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 7 becomes a 4 in the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
