29  \nBreakdown:  \nHundred thousands: 2  \nTen thousands: 0  \nThousands: 7  \nHundreds: 8  \nTens: 2  \nOnes: 9  \n\nSo adding digit by digit:\n\nOnes: 6 + 9 = 15 → 5, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9 → 9.\n\nHundreds: 0 + 8 = 8.\n\nThousands: 6 (from first) + 7 (from second) = 13 → 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 8 (from first) + 0 (from second) = 8 + 1 (carryover) = 9.\n\nHundred thousands place: 9 (from first) + 2 (from second) = 11 → 1 (digit) and carryover 1. Since there\'s no higher place, add that 1 as a new digit. So total becomes 1,193,895?\n\nWait, so the digits would be:\n\nMillions place: 1 (from the carryover).\n\nHundred thousands: 1 (since 9+2=11, so 1 in hundred thousands and carryover 1 to millions)\n\nWait, let me structure this properly.\n\nWait, the places are as follows:\n\nMillions (next after hundred thousands) would be the first digit here.\n\nWait, let\'s lay it out:\n\nWhen adding the hundred thousands digits: 9 (from 986,066) and 2 (from 207,829) add to 11. So we write down 1 in the hundred thousands place, and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there were no millions digits in either number, the carried over 1 becomes the millions digit. So the total is 1 (million) + 1 (hundred thousand) plus the rest.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nMillions place: 1\n\nHundred thousands: 1\n\nTen thousands: 9\n\nThousands: 3\n\nHundreds: 8\n\nTens: 9\n\nOnes:5\n\nWait, that would be 1,193,895? Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n986,066 + 207,829.\n\nLet me compute 986,066 + 200,000 = 1,186,066\n\nThen add 7,829: 1,186,066 + 7,829 = 1,193,895. Yes, that matches.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,193,895.\n\nWait, but in my initial steps, when I broke down each digit, the digits after each place were:\n\nOnes:5\n\nTens:9\n\nHundreds:8\n\nThousands:3 (with carryover 1)\n\nTen thousands:9 (from 8+0 +1 carried over)\n\nHundred thousands: 1 (from 9+2=11, so 1 in hundred thousands and carryover 1 to