usands place: 0 + 3 = 3, plus 1 = 4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place: 3 + 1 = 4. Write 4.\n\nHundred thousands place: 9 + 3 = 12. Write 2, carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNow, since there\'s a carryover of 1 to the millions place, which wasn\'t there before, so the total is 1,244,721?\n\nWait let me write all the digits step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 5+6=11 → 1, carry 1.\n\nTens:7+4=11 +1=12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:9+7=16 +1=17 → 7, carry 1.\n\nThousands:0+3=3 +1=4 → 4, carry 0.\n\nTen thousands:3+1=4 → 4.\n\nHundred thousands:9+3=12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nMillions place: carryover 1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:2\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:4\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nMillions:1.\n\nSo putting it all together: 1,244,721.\n\nWait let me check with another method. Let\'s add them numerically:\n\n930,975\n\n+313,746\n\n________\n\nLet\'s add:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +6 =11, so 1, carryover 1.\n\n7+4 =11 +1=12 → 2, carryover1.\n\n9+7=16 +1=17 →7, carryover1.\n\n0+3=3 +1=4.\n\n3+1=4.\n\n9+3=12 →2 carryover1.\n\nThen the million place:1.\n\nSo the total is 1,244,721.\n\nHmm, but let me verify with another way. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n930,975 + 300,000 = 1,230,975.\n\nThen add 13,746 to that:\n\n1,230,975 +13,746 = 1,244,721. Yes, that matches.\n\nSo the final answer should be 1,244,721.\n\nWait, but let me check again with digit-by-digit steps to ensure I didn\'t make any mistake.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n\u2003930,975\n\n+313,746\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n5 +6=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nTens place:7+4=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:9+7=16 +1=17 →7, carryover1.\n\nThousands place:0 +3=3 +1=4 →4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands:3 (from first number) +1 (second number)=4 →4.\n\nHundred thousands:9 +3=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 2 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 4 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 2 (ten), 1 (one). So 1,244,721. Yes, that seems correct.\n\nWait, but the user\'s original question had the numbers as 930975 and 313746. Let me confirm the digits again. 930,975 is nine hundred thirty thousand, nine hundred seventy-five. 313,746 is three hundred thirteen thousand, seven hundred forty-six. Adding those gives the total I found. So I think that\'s correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 1,244,721.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 930975 and 313746 is \\boxed{1244721}.\n'] 26%|##5       | 128/500 [2:33:39<5:27:04, 52.75s/it]
