us 1 carried over is 14. So write 4 and carryover 1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover becomes a new digit in the millions place: 1.\n\nSo putting all the digits together:\n\nMillions:1, Hundred thousands:4, Ten thousands:3, Thousands:8, Hundreds:9, Tens:3, Ones:6.\n\nTherefore the total is 1,438,936.\n\nWait, but let me check again step by step:\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n      460552\n    +978384\n    ---------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 +4 =6\n\nTens:5 +8=13. So 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:5+3=8 +1=9.\n\nThousands place:0+8=8 (no carryover).\n\nTen thousands:6 +7=13. So 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +9=13 plus 1=14. So 4 in the hundred thousands place, carryover 1 to the millions.\n\nSo the total is 1,438,936.\n\nHmm, so the answer should be 1,438,936. Let me confirm with another method. Let's add 460,552 + 978,384.\n\nAlternatively, adding 460,552 + 978,384:\n\nFirst, 460,552 + 900,000 = 1,360,552\n\nThen add 78,384: 1,360,552 +70,000 = 1,430,552\n\nThen 8,384 more: 1,430,552 +8,384 = 1,438,936. Yes, that matches.\n\nTherefore the correct answer is 1,438,936.\n\nWait, but in the initial problem statement, the numbers were 460552 and 978384. So the user wants the sum of those two numbers. Let me make sure I didn't misread the numbers. 460,552 is correct (four hundred sixty thousand five hundred fifty-two) and 978,384 is nine hundred seventy-eight thousand three hundred eighty-four. Yes, so adding them gives 1,438,936. So the final answer is 1,438,936.\n"]
