). Wait, hold on, let me check again because I might have messed up the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out more systematically. Let's line them up:.\n\n  911,213.\n+ 252,553.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 9 + 9 = 25. Write 0, carryover 2. So ones digit is 0.\n\nTens: 8 + 1 = 67 + 4 = 54. Write 7, carryover 8. Tens digit is 2.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 4 = 0 + 5 (carryover) = 9. Hundreds digit is 6, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 4 + 1 = 1. Thousands digit is 5.\n\nTen thousands: 0 (from first number) + 4 (from second) = 93. So here we have 70. Wait, but ten thousands place: the first number has 7 in the ten thousands place (since 948,253 is 7 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands)), yes. The second number is 058,524 which is 0 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands). So adding 4 + 0 = 67. So we write 7 in the ten thousands place and carry over 5 to the hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands place: 5 + 4 = 49, plus the carried over 7 makes 62. So write 5 in the hundred thousands and carry over 0 to the millions place. The millions place is just the carried over 4. .\n\nSo putting all the digits together: 0 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 3 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
