 out step by step more carefully. Let me try again:.\n\nNumbers are:.\n\n  685090.\n+ 311014.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 9 + 9 = 6. Correct.\n\nTens: 1 +9 =2. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 4 +2 =20. So 1, carryover 4.\n\nThousands place: The first number has 3 (from 858,030: the thousands digit is the fourth from the right, which is 5?), wait maybe I need to check the digit positions again.\n\nWait, let me write the numbers with commas for clarity:.\n\n660,939 is 3 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\n788,912 is 4 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo aligning:.\n\n        8 0 2 5 3 5.\n      + 0 5 1 1 6 0.\n      ----------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n9+1=2 (ones place).\n\nTens: 0+7=7 (tens place).\n\nHundreds:9+9=40. Write 1, carryover 3.\n\nThousands place:2 (from first number) +6 (from second) =36, plus the carried 7 makes 42. So write 2 here and carryover 6.\n\nTen-thousands place:7 (from first number) +1 (from second) =21, plus carried 5 is 96. Write 5, carryover 9.\n\nHundred-thousands place:1 (from first) +7 (from second)=27, plus carried 4 is 36. So write 7 here and carryover 9 to the millions place.\n\nSo the total would be 9 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
