4 (first) +3 (second)=66 +2=84 →5, carryover8.\n\nHundred thousands place:4 (first) +5 (second)=47 +3=49 →1, carryover8?.\n\nWait, but the hundred thousands place addition would be 0+0=36, plus the carryover 5 gives 45. So that would be 5 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 9 to the millions place. But since both numbers are six digits, adding them could result in a seven-digit number. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
