gain.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The first number has a 7, the second a 5, plus the carried 9: 6 + 3 + 0 = 52. So that's 7 in the hundred thousands place and 3 carried over to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 0 becomes the millions digit.\n\nPutting all together: 2 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (ones). Wait, let me check that again. Wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me recount step by step.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out more carefully. Let's see:.\n\n903,873.\n+428,930.\n----------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6 +0=62 → 4, carry 9.\n\nTens:3+3=90, plus 7 is 55 → 0, carry 0.\n\nHundreds:1+0=32, plus 6=96 →6, carry8.\n\nThousands:1 (from 938,226) + 2 (from 639,165) = 32, plus 6 is 73 →2, carry7.\n\nWait, hold on, the thousands digit in 485,976 is 4? Let me confirm the place values again. Let's break down each number:.\n\n245,567:.\n- 1 (hundred thousands).\n- 7 (ten thousands).\n- 2 (thousands).\n- 3 (hundreds).\n- 8 (tens).\n- 1 (ones).\n\n101,107:.\n- 5 (hundred thousands).\n- 3 (ten thousands).\n- 8 (thousands).\n- 4 (hundreds).\n- 1 (tens).\n- 7 (ones).\n\nSo when adding the thousands place: 2 (from first number) + 8 (from second) = 53, plus the carryover 5 gives 84. So write 0 in thousands place, carryover 0.\n\nThen ten thousands place: first number has 4, second has 5 → 3+6=2, plus the carried 3 makes 97 → write 6, carryover 6.\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 +4 =76, plus the carried 2 is 77 → write 0 and carryover 8. Since there's no higher place, that 8 becomes a new digit in the millions place.\n\nPutting all together, the digits from right to left are:.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nMillions:6. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
