s no higher place, the 9 is added as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right: 4 (ones), 9 (tens), 7 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), then 36 in the hundred thousands. Wait, no, let me retrace. Wait, maybe I messed up the order of the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, perhaps I should list each digit's place step by step again to make sure:.\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned properly:.\n\n      2 2 6 2 0 2.\n    + 7 5 5 1 8 6.\n    ---------------.\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 7 +3 =1. Write 4.\n\nTens:3 +8=77. Write 8, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds:5 +4=6, plus the carried 3 makes 6. Write 2.\n\nThousands:5 +3=8. Write 6.\n\nTen-thousands:4 +1=83. Write 0, carryover 4.\n\nHundred-thousands:6 +2=66, plus the carried 6 makes 66. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 0 (from first number) plus 2 (second number) is 32, plus the carried 7 is 21. So the hundred-thousands place is 9, and carryover 0 to the millions place. So the total would be 0 (million) 1 (hundred thousand), etc. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
