 + 90 = 160 → 1,513,860.\n\nFinally, 4 +5 =9 → 1,513,869. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer should be 1,513,869. I think in my first attempt I messed up the digit positions. So the correct reasoning step by step is as follows:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digits (ones place):\n\n1. Ones place: 4 + 5 = 9\n2. Tens place: 7 + 9 = 16 (write 6, carryover 1)\n3. Hundreds place: 4 + 3 + 1 (carryover) = 8\n4. Thousands place: 6 + 7 = 13 (write 3, carryover 1)\n5. Ten-thousands place: 7 + 3 + 1 (carryover) = 11 (write 1, carryover 1)\n6. Hundred-thousands place: 8 + 6 + 1 (carryover) = 15 (write 5, carryover 1)\n7. Millions place: the carryover 1.\n\nThus, combining all gives 1,513,869. I need to make sure each step is clear in the reasoning.\n"]
