he hundred thousands? Wait, no, the hundred thousands place addition is separate. Wait, let me go step by step again.\n\nLet me do the addition step by step again carefully:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes place:.\n6 + 5 = 5. Write down 5.\n\nTens place:.\n4 + 7 = 03. Write down 0, carryover 4 to the hundreds.\n\nHundreds place:.\n5 + 0 = 28, plus the carried 9 is 48. Write down 6, carryover 6.\n\nThousands place:.\n7 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) = 5, plus the carried 7 = 7. Write down 0. No carryover here.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n2 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 5. Write down 0. No carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n6 (from first number) + 3 (from second number) = 65. Write down 91.\n\nSo putting all the digits together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:6, Tens:6, Hundreds:0, Thousands:2, Ten thousands:4, Hundred thousands:33.\n\nWait, but writing it out, the hundred thousands place is 27, so the total number would be 70 followed by the other digits. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
