 Here, we write down 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nSince there are no more digits, the carried over 1 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nThe sum is 1 (millions) 3 (hundred thousands) 6 (ten thousands) 3 (thousands) 3 (hundreds) 5 (tens) 9 (ones). So that\'s 1,363,359.\n\nWait, let me verify again step by step.\n\nBreaking down each digit:\n\nFirst number: 432,120\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nOnes: 0\n\nTens: 2\n\nHundreds: 1\n\nThousands: 2\n\nTen thousands: 3\n\nHundred thousands: 4\n\nSecond number: 931,239\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nOnes:9\n\nTens:3\n\nHundreds:2\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nNow adding each column:\n\nOnes: 0 + 9 =9\n\nTens: 2 +3=5\n\nHundreds:1+2=3\n\nThousands:2+1=3\n\nTen thousands:3+3=6\n\nHundred thousands:4+9=13\n\nSo the hundred thousands column gives 13, which is 3 in that place and carryover 1 to millions.\n\nSo the total is 1,363,359.\n\nWait, that seems correct. Let me confirm by another method. Maybe adding using place values:\n\n432,120 can be written as 400,000 + 30,000 + 2,000 + 100 + 20 + 0\n\n931,239 is 900,000 + 30,000 + 1,000 + 200 + 30 +9\n\nAdding them:\n\n400,000 + 900,000 = 1,300,000\n\n30,000 + 30,000 =60,000\n\n2,000 +1,000=3,000\n\n100 +200=300\n\n20 +30=50\n\n0+9=9\n\nAdding all those together:\n\n1,300,000 +60,000 =1,360,000\n\n1,360,000 +3,000=1,363,000\n\n1,363,000 +300=1,363,300\n\n1,363,300 +50=1,363,350\n\n1,363,350 +9=1,363,359\n\nYes, that matches. So the sum is indeed 1,363,359.\n\nWait a second, but in the initial calculation when I first started thinking, I had some confusion with different numbers, but now focusing on the correct problem, it\'s clear. So the reasoning steps are as above. The answer is 1,363,359.\n\nBut let me also check using another method, like calculator style:\n\n432,120 + 931,239.\n\nAdding 432,120 + 900,000 = 1,332,120\n\nThen add 31,239 to that:\n\n1,332,120 + 31,239 = 1,363,359. Yep, same result.\n\nOk