ace: 4 + 3 = 7 plus 1 →8. Write 8.\n\nHundreds place: 6 + 0 =6 → write 6.\n\nThousands place: 6 +8 =14 → write 4, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 0 +9 =9 plus 1 →10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 +8 =16 plus 1 →17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: the carried over 1. So total is 1,704,684?\n\nWait let me verify each step again carefully:\n\nFirst, align the numbers properly:\n\n806649\n\n+898035\n\nEach digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 9 (from first) +5 (second) =14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 4 +3 =7 plus 1 is 8. So 8, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place:6 +0 =6.\n\nThousands place:6 +8 =14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:0 +9 =9 plus the carried 1 →10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:8 (from first number\'s hundred thousands digit) +8 (second number\'s hundred thousands digit) =16, plus the carried 1 →17. So write 7 and carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: The first number has no millions digit, so it\'s 0. The second number also has 8 in hundred thousands, so no millions digit. But we have a carried over 1. So that becomes the millions digit. So putting it all together:\n\nThe digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:4\n\nTens:8\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:4\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nMillions:1\n\nSo the number is 1,704,684?\n\nWait, let\'s see:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nMillions place:1\n\nHundred thousands:7 → so 1,7\n\nTen thousands:0 → 1,70\n\nThousands:4 → 1,704\n\nHundreds:6 → 1,704,6\n\nTens:8 → 1,704,68\n\nOnes:4 → 1,704,684.\n\nYes, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding 806,649 + 898,035:\n\nLet me add 800,000 + 800,000 = 1,600,000. Then the remaining parts:\n\n6,649 +98,035 = 104,684. So total is 1,600,000 +104,684=1,704,684. Yep, matches.\n\nSo the correct answer is 1,704,684.\n\nEarlier confusion was because I was looking at a different problem, but now focusing on the correct numbers. So the reasoning should be step by step adding each digit with carries as