nd has a 0. Adding those: 5 +8 =43. So that's 8 and 9, meaning 77. So we write 0 in the hundred thousands place and carry over another 7, but since there are no more digits, that 8 becomes a new digit at the beginning. Wait, but actually, both numbers only have up to the hundred thousands place. Wait, 043942 is a six-digit number, so 7 is in the hundred thousands place. The second number is 048,039, which is also six digits, so 8 in the hundred thousands. Adding 3 +4 gives 49, so we write 3 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 0 to the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
