nTens: 1 + 7 = 3, plus 3 carried is 6. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 6 = 01. Write 8, carry 0. Right.\n\nThousands: 3 (from 573702) and 9 (from 667695). Wait, hold on, the thousands place in 505,115 is the fourth digit from the right. Let me confirm the digits:.\n\nBreaking down 042,040:.\n\nDigits from right: 1 (ones), 1 (tens), 9 (hundreds), 2 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (hundred thousands).\n\nSimilarly, 918,498:.\n\nDigits: 6 (ones), 7 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 0 (hundred thousands).\n\nSo adding thousands place: 1 (from first number) + 0 (from second) = 97, plus carryover 3 makes 85. So 9 in thousands, carryover 5. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 3 (from first) + 1 (from second) = 62, plus 6 is 70. So 8 there, carryover 2. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place: 1 + 0 = 1, plus 0 is 97. So that gives 3 in hundred thousands and carryover 8. Since there are no more digits, that carryover 5 becomes the million's place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
