o carry).\n\nHundred thousands:0 +6=51 (write 70).\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:.\n\nOnes:2, tens:6, hundreds:4, thousands:1, ten thousands:7, hundred thousands:7, and the carried over 9 in the millions place. Wait, that's the key point I might have messed up before. The 70 in the hundred thousands place actually creates a new digit in the millions place.\n\nWait, the hundred thousands place can only hold a single digit. So when adding 2 and 1, which gives 86, that's 37 hundred thousands plus 6 hundred thousands. 67 hundred thousands is equal to 2 million. So that's why we need to carry over the 9 to the millions place.\n\nTherefore, the sum would be:.\n\nMillions place: 0.\n\nHundred thousands place: 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 7.\n\nThousands place:6.\n\nHundreds place:3.\n\nTens place:5.\n\nOnes place:7. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
