ches. So the correct answer is 1,145,866.\n\nWait, but the initial problem was 879,974 and 265,892. Let me check the addition again:\n\n879,974\n\n+265,892\n\n=?\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4 +2 =6.\n\nTens:7+9=16, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:9+8=17 +1=18, carryover1.\n\nThousands:9+5=14 +1=15, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:7+6=13 +1=14, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:8+2=10 +1=11, carryover1.\n\nMillions: 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,145,866. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning should follow these steps, digit by digit.\n"]
