ight (ones place):\n\n0 +9 =9.\n\nTens place: 6 +1 =7.\n\nHundreds place: 9 +8 =17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from first number) +3 (second number) + carried 1 =4.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 (first) +1 (second) =1.\n\nHundred-thousands place:5 +3=8.\n\nWait, let me do step by step properly:\n\nOnes place: 0 +9 =9.\n\nTens place:6 +1=7.\n\nHundreds place:9 (from first number\'s hundreds) +8 (second number\'s hundreds) =17. So write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:0 (first number\'s thousands) +3 (second number\'s thousands) +1 (carryover) =4. So 4 in thousands place, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place:0 (first number\'s ten-thousands) +1 (second number\'s ten-thousands) =1. \n\nHundred-thousands place:5 (first number) +3 (second) =8.\n\nPutting all together: 8 (hundred-thousands), 1 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 9 (ones). So the total is 814,779?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the thousands place:\n\nWait, first number\'s thousands digit is the fourth from the right. Let\'s write each digit with their places:\n\nFirst number: 500,960 is 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 313,819 is 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones).\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes:0+9=9\n\nTens:6+1=7\n\nHundreds:9+8=17 → write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:0 +3 +1(carry)=4\n\nTen-thousands:0 +1=1\n\nHundred-thousands:5+3=8.\n\nThus the total is 814,779.\n\nWait, but let me verify by another method. Let\'s add them:\n\n500,960 + 313,819.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n500,000 + 300,000 = 800,000\n\n0 (ten thousands) +10,000 =10,000 → total so far 810,000\n\n0 (thousands) +3,000 =3,000 → 813,000\n\n9 hundreds +8 hundreds =17 hundreds → 1,700 → total 814,700\n\n60 +10 =70 → 814,770\n\nPlus the remaining 9 (from the ones place?) Wait, no, the ones were already added as 0+9=9. Wait, perhaps better to compute:\n\n500,960 +313,819:\n