 (hundred thousands) column.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n\n3 (first) +3 (second) =59, plus the carried over 7 → 41. So we write 1 and carryover 5 to the millions place.\n\nSo the hundred thousands digit is 0, and the carryover 6 becomes the millions digit. So the digits are:.\n\nMillions place:6.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:4.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nTens:4.\n\nOnes:8. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
