its: 1 (million), 0 (hundred thousand), 5 (ten thousand), 3 (thousand), 3 (hundred), 8 (ten), 8 (one). So 1,053,388. That seems right. But the original numbers are 122,758 and 930,630. Let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as:\n\n122,758 + 900,000 = 1,022,758. Then add 30,630: 1,022,758 + 30,630 = 1,053,388. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer should be 1,053,388. I think I made a mistake in my initial steps because I was mixing up digits, but this step-by-step approach works better.\n</think>\n\n",
