ousands: 2\n- Thousands: 7\n- Hundreds: 0\n- Tens: 3\n- Ones: 6\n\nSecond number: 320,153 is:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 3\n- Ten thousands: 2\n- Thousands: 0\n- Hundreds: 1\n- Tens: 5\n- Ones: 3\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes: 6 + 3 = 9 → 9\n\nTens: 3 + 5 = 8 → 8\n\nHundreds: 0 + 1 = 1 → 1\n\nThousands: 7 + 0 = 7 →7\n\nTen thousands: 2 + 2 =4 →4\n\nHundred thousands:9 +3 =12 →2, carryover 1\n\nMillions place: carryover 1 →1\n\nSo the total is 1,247,189?\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\n927,036 + 320,153:\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\n927,036 + 300,000 = 1,227,036\n\nThen add 20,000 → 1,247,036\n\nThen add 153 → 1,247,036 + 153 = 1,247,189. Yes, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, another way:\n\n927,036\n\n+320,153\n\n= (900,000 + 27,036) + (300,000 + 20,153)\n\n= (900,000 + 300,000) + (27,036 + 20,153)\n\n= 1,200,000 + 47,189 = 1,247,189.\n\nYes, so the sum is 1,247,189.\n\nWait, but let me check the digits again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6+3=9 ✔️\n\nTens:3+5=8 ✔️\n\nHundreds:0+1=1 ✔️\n\nThousands:7+0=7 ✔️\n\nTen thousands:2+2=4 ✔️\n\nHundred thousands:9+3=12 → so write 2, carryover 1. Then the millions place is 1. So total is 1,247,189. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 1,247,189.\n\nBut let me ensure there was no miscalculation in the addition steps. Maybe I should do it the standard column addition way:\n\n\u202f 927,036\n\n+ 320,153\n\n------------\n\nStart adding each column from right to left:\n\nOnes column: 6 + 3 = 9. Write 9.\n\nTens column: 3 + 5 = 8. Write 8.\n\nHundreds column: 0 + 1 = 1. Write 1.\n\nThousands column:7 + 0 =7. Write 7.\n\nTen thousands column:2 + 2 =4. Write 4.\n\nHundred thousands column:9 +3 =12. Write 2 and carryover 1.\n\nMillions column: The carried over 1, so write 1.\n\nPutting it all together: 1,247,189. Yep, that\'s correct.\n\nSo the final answer is 1,247,189.\n'] 62%|######2   | 312/500 [6:43:30<3:32:33, 67.84s/it]
