02,067:\n\nDigits from right:\n\nOnes:7\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:0\n\nThousands:2\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nSimilarly, 798,751:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:5\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:8\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nSo when adding thousands place: 2 (from first number) +8 (from second) = 10. Wait! Here's the mistake. I thought the thousands digit of the second number was 7? No, wait:\n\nWait let's re-express:\n\nFirst number: 302,067\n\nBreakdown:\n\nHundred thousands: 3\n\nTen thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 2\n\nHundreds: 0\n\nTens: 6\n\nOnes: 7\n\nSecond number: 798,751\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:7\n\nTens:5\n\nOnes:1\n\nSo when adding the thousands place: first number has 2, second has 8 → 2 +8 =10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nAh! That's where I messed up before. So in the thousands place, it's 2 +8 =10, not 2+7. The hundreds place is 0 +7 +1 (carryover) =8.\n\nWait, let's redo the addition properly:\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes:7 +1 =8\n\nTens:6 +5 =11 → 1, carryover1\n\nHundreds:0 +7 =7 +1 (carryover) =8 → write 8, no carryover.\n\nThousands:2 +8 =10 → write 0, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:0 +9 =9 +1 (carryover) =10 → write 0, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +7 =10 +1 (carryover) =11 → write 11?\n\nWait:\n\nWait, let's go step by step:\n\n1. Ones place: 7 +1 =8. Write 8.\n\n2. Tens:6 +5 =11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\n3. Hundreds:0 (from first) +7 (from second) =7 +1 (carryover)=8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\n4. Thousands:2 (first) +8 (second) =10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands:0 (first) +9 (second)=9 +1 (carryover)=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:3 (first) +7 (second)=10 +1 (carryover)=11. So here we have to write 1 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. Since there's no higher place, the total becomes 1,100,0 (from hundred thousands) plus the rest?\n\nWait, the digits would be:\n\nAfter all steps:\n\nThe digits from right to left:\n\nOnes:8\n\nTens:1\n\nHundreds:8\n\nThousands:0\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:1 (with a carryover 1 to millions)\n\nSo the total is 1 (million) 1 (hundred thousands) 0 (ten thousands) 0 (thousands) 8 (hundreds) 1 (tens) 8 (ones). So that's 1,100,818. Which matches the second method. So my first mistake was in the thousands place where I incorrectly added 2+7 instead of 2+8. So the correct answer is 1,100,818.\n\nWait, let me confirm with another method:\n\n302,067 + 798,751.\n\nLet's subtract 1 from the second number to make it 798,750, which is easier, then add back 1 later.\n\n302,067 + 798,750 = ?\n\n302,067 + 700,000 = 1,002,067\n\nThen add 98,750: 1,002,067 + 98,750 = 1,100,817\n\nThen add back the 1: 1,100,818. Yep, same result. So the correct sum is 1,100,818.\n\nSo the initial step-by-step had an error in the thousands place, leading to confusion, but correcting that gives the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 302,067 and 798,751 is \\boxed{1100818}.\n"] 70%|#######   | 352/500 [7:27:59<2:35:26, 63.02s/it]
