ng it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6.\n\nTens: 1 (with a carryover).\n\nHundreds: 0 (with a carryover).\n\nThousands: 0.\n\nTen-thousands: 1.\n\nHundred-thousands: 9 (plus the carryover from the hundred-thousands addition).\n\nAnd then the new millions digit from the carryover: 6. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
