ave messed up the positions.\n\nWait, let me write it step by step properly:.\n\nLet me align them properly:.\n\n      9 7 7 9 0 4.\n    + 8 4 8 5 8 2.\n    ----------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 6 + 9 = 7. Write down 6.\n\nTens: 1 + 2 = 8. Write 5.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 2 = 3. Write 3.\n\nThousands: 6 + 7 = 5. Write 7.\n\nTen-thousands: 9 + 3 = 90. Write 3, carryover 8.\n\nHundred-thousands: 9 + 6 = 05, plus the carried 2 is 32. So write 0 here and carryover 4.\n\nSince there's a carryover, we add a new digit at the millions place: 8.\n\nSo putting all together, the sum is 6 (million), 9 (hundred-thousands), 9 (ten-thousands), 5 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 2 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
