second, let me check if there are any more digits. The first number is 492,609 which has six digits, and the second is 236,889 which also has six digits. So I think that's all the places. Let me add them again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 2 = 43 (write 4, carry 7).\nTens: 7 + 0 + 4 (carry) = 7.\nHundreds: 1 + 3 = 0.\nThousands: 4 + 2 = 7.\nTen-thousands: 6 + 9 = 62 (write 7, carry 5).\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 2 + 3 (carry) = 8.\n\nPutting it all together, the digits from right to left are 5 (ones), 8 (tens), 2 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 3 (hundred-thousands). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
