w digit at the millions place.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4\n\nTens:8\n\nHundreds:5\n\nThousands:4\n\nTen thousands:1 (with a carryover of 1)\n\nHundred thousands: (8+4=12 +1=13 → 3 and carry 1)\n\nMillions place: the carried over 1.\n\nTherefore the total is 1,286,384?\n\nWait, let me check step by step again.\n\nWait let me write each digit:\n\nNumber1: 873,273\n\nBreaking down digit by digit:\n\nFrom right to left:\n\n1. Ones: 3\n\n2. Tens:7\n\n3. Hundreds:2\n\n4. Thousands:3 (since it\'s 873,273, so the thousands digit is the fourth from the right, which is 3)\n\nWait, wait, let\'s parse the number correctly.\n\nLet me write 873,273 as:\n\nDigits:\n\nMillions: 0 (since it\'s a 6-digit number)\n\nHundred thousands: 8\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:3\n\nWait, commas are placed every three digits. So 873,273 is 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 3 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 413,111:\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:1\n\nSo writing them vertically:\n\nHundred thousands Ten thousands Thousands Hundreds Tens Ones\n\n873,273: 8    7      3       2     7    3\n\n+413,111: 4    1      3       1     1    1\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 3 +1 =4\n\nTens:7 +1 =8\n\nHundreds:2 +1 =3\n\nThousands:3 +3 =6\n\nTen thousands:7 +1 =8\n\nHundred thousands:8 +4 =12\n\nWait, so the total would be 12 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (ones). But 12 in hundred thousands place is actually 1,200,000. So the total would be 1,286,384?\n\nWait, let me check:\n\nWait, let me add step by step:\n\nStart with the ones column:\n\nOnes:3 +1 =4. Write 4.\n\nTens:7 +1 =8. Write 8.\n\nHundreds:2 +1 =3. Write 3.\n\nThousands:3 (from first number) +3 (from second) =6. Write 6.\n\nTen thousands:7 +1 =8. Write 8.\n\nHundred thousands:8 +4 =12. So write 2 and carry over 1 to the millions 