t, hold on, let me check again step by step because I might have messed up the places.\n\nWait, maybe I should do it step by step vertically. Let me try again:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes column: 6 + 0 = 33. So 9, carryover 9.\n\nTens column: 4 + 5 = 64, plus 9 is 38. So 0, carryover 7.\n\nHundreds column: 6 + 1 = 00, plus 0 is 96. So 2, carryover 2.\n\nThousands column: 4 (from first number) +4 (from second number) = 7, plus 0 carried over is 5. So 2, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands column: 9 (from first number) +1 (from second) = 5. So 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands column: 9 +6 =68. So 4 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 9 to millions place. Wait, but 8+7 is 92, so actually, the hundred thousands place becomes 9 and we have a 5 in the millions place. .\n\nSo putting it all together, the total sum is 5 (millions) 9 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
