\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 0 = 7. Write down 7.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 5 = 10. Write 0 and carry over 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 9 + 5 = 14, plus the carried 1 is 15. So write 5 and carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 3 + 8 = 11, plus carried 1 is 12. So write 2 and carry over 1. But since there\'s no higher place, we need to add that 1 as a new digit.\n\nWait, so that would make the total 1,250, 807?\n\nWait, let me do it step by step:\n\nAdding the thousands place: 5 (from first) + 5 (from second) = 10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 9 + 5 =14, plus the 1 gives 15. So write 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 3 +8 =11, plus 1 is 12. So we write 2 and carryover 1. Since there are no more digits, that carried over 1 becomes a new digit at the million place. So total digits would be 1 (million) 2 (hundred thousand) 5 (ten thousand), etc. Wait, maybe I need to track all digits:\n\nLet me write each step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 5 + 2 = 7. Ones digit is 7.\n\nTens: 1 +8=9. Tens is 9.\n\nHundreds:7 +0=7. Hundreds digit 7.\n\nThousands:5 +5=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:9 +5=14 +1=15. So digit 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +8=11 +1=12. So digit 2, carryover 1.\n\nNow, the million place: the carryover 1. So that\'s an extra digit.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 1 (million) 2 (hundred thousand), 5 (ten thousand), 0 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 9 (ten), 7 (one). Wait, let me see:\n\nWait the digits from right to left:\n\nOnes:7\n\nTens:9\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:0\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nMillions:1\n\nSo writing that out, it\'s 1,250,797?\n\nWait that doesn\'t match my earlier thought. Let me check the thousands place again.\n\nWait, let\'s write the addition vertically:\n\n      395,715\n    +855,082\n    ----------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5+2=7\n\nTens:1+8=9\n\nHundreds:7+0=7\n\nThousands:5+5=10 (write 0, carryover 1)\n\nTen thousands:9+5=14 +1=15 (write 5, carryover1)