as the new digit. So putting it all together, the millions place is 3, then the hundred-thousands is 2, ten-thousands is 9, thousands is 6, hundreds is 9, tens 8, ones 6. Wait, let me check again step by step.\n\nWait, let me do this again more carefully to avoid mistakes:.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:.\n\n\u202f046634.\n\n+733233.\n\n----------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\nOnes place: 5 + 7 = 53. Write 6, carryover 4.\n\nTens place: 8 + 6 = 4, plus the 8 carried over is 0. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 9 = 05. Write 9, carryover 3.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 4 = 4, plus 3 carried over = 4. Write 0, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 + 7 = 0. Write 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 8 = 92. Write 6 and carryover 8.\n\nNow, since we have a carryover from the hundred-thousands, we add a new digit (millions place): 2.\n\nSo putting all together: 0 (million), 1 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 3 (hundred), 4 (ten), 8 (one). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
