ny digits.\n\nWait, let me redo the places carefully:.\n\nLet me write each digit in columns:.\n\n        4 8 6 0 7 2.\n      + 8 5 7 7 3 8.\n      ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 2 +2 =6.\n\nTens: 1 +8=09 (carry 6, write 5).\n\nHundreds:6 (from first) +3 (second) +0 (carry) =4.\n\nThousands:3 (first) +8 (second) =93 (carry 9, write 3).\n\nTen thousands:4 +6 =0 plus the carryover 9 makes 0.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +6=82 (carryover 7, write 8).\n\nThen the carryover 7 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo the total is 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands),8 (hundreds),5 (tens),7 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
