\nTens: 4 +6 =31. Write 3, carryover 8.\n\nHundreds:9 +5 =00, plus 6 carried over is 88. Write 5, carryover 8.\n\nThousands:5 +0 =94, plus 6 =49. Write 7, carryover 5.\n\nTen thousands:7 +9 =5, plus 7 carried over =6. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +0 =41. Write 35.\n\nSo putting all digits together:.\n\nThe result is 65 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 3 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
