ryover from hundreds) =13. So write 3, carryover1? Wait no, wait that contradicts my previous step. Let me re-express:\n\nWait step-by-step:\n\n1. Ones place (units):\n\n9 +6 =15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\n2. Tens place:\n\n8 +5 =13 \u219213 +1 (carryover) =14 \u21924, carryover1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:\n\n7 +7 =14 \u219214 +1 (carryover) =15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\n4. Thousands place:\n\n6 (from first number's thousands) +6 (second's thousands) =12 \u219212 +1 (carryover) =13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:\n\n7 (first's ten thousands) +3 (second's ten thousands) =10 \u219210 +1 (carryover) =11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:\n\n5 (first's hundred thousands) +8 (second's hundred thousands) =13 \u219213 +1 (carryover) =14 \u21924, carryover1.\n\n7. Then the carryover1 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo the result is:\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:4\n\nOnes:5\n\nPutting it all together: 1,413,545.\n\nWait, so the total is 1,413,545.\n\nLet me verify with another method. Let's add the numbers:\n\n576,789 + 836,756.\n\nAdding 500k +800k =1,300,000.\n\nThen 76,789 +36,756.\n\n76k +36k =112k.\n\n789 +756 =1,545.\n\nSo total is 1,300,000 +112,000 =1,412,000 +1,545 =1,413,545. That matches. So the correct answer is 1,413,545.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning steps need to be written out as per the template. Let me structure it properly:\n\nThe question is the sum of 576789 and 836756.\n\nReasoning:\n\n1. Ones place: 9 +6 =15. Write down 5, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens place:8 +5 =13 +1 =14. Write 4, carryover1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:7 +7 =14 +1 =15. Write5, carryover1.\n\n4. Thousands place:6 +6 =12 +1 =13. Write3, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:7 +3 =10 +1 =11. Write1, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:5 +8 =13 +1 =14. Write4, carryover1.\n\n7. Millions place: carryover1.\n\nThus, combining all digits gives 1,413,545.\n\nAnswer: Therefore, the final computed sum is 1413545.\n\nWait, but in the template, the answer is written as <<answer>>. So need to present it in the boxed format as per instructions.\n</think>\n\n",
