 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:9 +8=17 plus 1 carried over is 18. So write 8, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: There's the carried over 1, so that's 1.\n\nPutting it all together: 1,854,292. Okay, that's correct. So I had a mistake in my first step-by-step when I thought the thousands place added to 68, that was wrong. The correct addition is 1,854,292.\n\nWait, but the user's question was about 142686 and 649636. Oh wait, I was solving a different problem in my head. Let me check again. The user's actual question is to add 142,686 and 649,636. I need to focus on that now. Let me start over.\n\nAlright, the problem is 142,686 plus 649,636. Let's align them:\n\n142686\n\n+649636\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n\u2003142686\n\n+649636\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\nOnes: 6 +6 =12. Write down 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 8 +3 =11 plus the carried 1 is 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:6 +6 =12 plus 1 is 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:2 +9 =11 plus 1 is 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:4 +4 =8 plus 1 is 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:1 +6 =7. Write 7.\n\nPutting all together: 792,322. Wait, let me check each step again.\n\nWait, let me write each digit step by step properly.\n\nFirst number: 142,686 can be broken down as:\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nPlace: Ones:6\n\nTens:8\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:2\n\nTen-thousands:4\n\nHundred-thousands:1\n\nSecond number:649,636:\n\nOnes:6\n\nTens:3\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:9\n\nTen-thousands:4\n\nHundred-thousands:6\n\nSo adding digit by digit:\n\nOnes:6+6=12 → 2, carryover 1\n\nTens:8+3=11 +1=12 → 2, carryover 1\n\nHundreds:6+6=12 +1=13 → 3, carryover1\n\nThousands:2+9=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1\n\nTen-thousands:4+4=8 +1=9 →9, no carryover\n\nHundred-thousands:1+6=7 →7\n\nSo total is 792,322. Let me confirm with another method.\n\nAdding 142,686 +649,636:\n\nFirst, 142,686 + 600,000 = 742,686\n\nThen add 49,636: 742,686 +