er 0 carried over to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 2 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits are 4 (ones), 2 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), then 4 (hundred-thousands), and the carried over 4 in the millions place. Wait, let me check again because I might have messed up the places.\n\nWait a second, maybe I should do this step-by-step more carefully. Let me write down each digit's place properly:.\n\nLet me align them again:.\n\n\u2003\u20036 3 5 8 1 9.\n+ 3 3 3 6 7 5.\n--------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 2 + 6 = 25 → 8, carryover 2.\n\nTens place: 0 + 5 = 84 + 4 = 42 → 3, carryover 2.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 9 = 8 + 8 (carryover) = 0 → 0, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 7 = 0 → 3, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 0 = 63 → 3, carryover 8.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 9 + 5 = 62 + 7 (carryover) = 40 → so here, the 0 is written in the hundred-thousands place and another 5 is carried over to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that becomes a 7 in the millions place.\n\nSo combining all digits from left to right: 9 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 8 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
