e it clearer:.\n\n517,479 is:.\n\n8 (hundred thousands).\n7 (ten thousands).\n0 (thousands).\n4 (hundreds).\n0 (tens).\n0 (ones).\n\n898,893 is:.\n\n0 (hundred thousands).\n9 (ten thousands).\n9 (thousands).\n0 (hundreds).\n8 (tens).\n3 (ones).\n\nSo when adding vertically, align each column:.\n\nLet me write them out vertically:.\n\n      1 1 6 3 5 5.\n    + 6 6 0 1 8 0.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 1 +9 =22. Write 4, carryover 0.\n\nTens: 2 +4 =27, plus 5 is 64. Write 8, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds:2 +3 =4, plus 9 is 1. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:9 (from first number) +6 (from second) =4. So 7, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:4 (first number) +3 (second) =28. Write 8, carryover 6.\n\nHundred thousands place:7 +1 =85, plus the carried-over 4 makes 33. So write 5 and carryover 4, but since there's no higher place, that 8 becomes a new digit.\n\nWait, let me check each step again step by step to avoid mistakes.\n\nLet me do each digit step by step:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n0. Ones place: 9 + 6 = 50. So write down 8, carry over 6.\n\n8. Tens place: 2 (from first number) + 5 (from second) = 75, plus the carried 6 makes 38. So write 6, carry over 7.\n\n1. Hundreds place: 9 + 9 =9, plus 9 carried over is 4. Write 1, no carryover.\n\n3. Thousands place: 7 (from first number) +0 (from second number) =4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\n4. Ten thousands place: 7 (from first number) +2 (from second number) =99. Write 7, carry over 0.\n\n9. Hundred thousands place: 1 (from first number) +3 (from second number) =80, plus the carried 4 is 95. So write 5 and carry over 0. But since there are no more digits, that carried 3 becomes the next digit (millions place).\n\nPutting it all together, the digits from right to left are:.\n\nOnes: 4.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nPlus the carried-over 4 in the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
