 should write it out step by step more carefully. Let me try adding each digit again, aligning properly:.\n\nLet me write each number with their place values:.\n\n937,876:.\n- Hundred thousands: 7.\n- Ten thousands: 5.\n- Thousands: 1.\n- Hundreds: 8.\n- Tens: 9.\n- Ones: 2.\n\n526,158:.\n- Hundred thousands: 6.\n- Ten thousands: 0.\n- Thousands: 5.\n- Hundreds: 6.\n- Tens: 1.\n- Ones: 8.\n\nAdding them digit by digit from right to left:.\n\nOnes place: 8 + 9 = 7. Write down 1.\n\nTens place: 4 + 1 = 8. Write down 4.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 3 = 9. Write down 9.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 1 = 68. Write down 0, carry over 5.\n\nTen thousands place: 3 + 2 + 8 (carry) = 77. Write down 2, carry over 0.\n\nHundred thousands place: 0 + 7 + 3 (carry) = 8. Write down 2. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
