), 8 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), and 5 (hundred thousands). Wait a second, let me check again because when I added the ten-thousands place, was that correct?.\n\nWait, let me go through each step again carefully to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me write them aligned:.\n\n      2 0 4 3 4 9.\n    + 5 6 8 9 6 8.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 8 + 6 = 30. Write 5, carryover 9. Correct.\n\nTens: 1 + 5 = 0, plus the 7 carried over is 0. So 1. Good.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 0 = 1. So 8. .\n\nThousands: 8 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 2. .\n\nTen-thousands: 6 (from first) + 4 (from second) = 3. .\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 2 = 2. .\n\nSo combining all the digits: 1 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 3 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
