k that again.\n\nWait a second, maybe I made a mistake in the thousands place. Let me go through each step again carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nNumbers:.\n\n\u2003137,210.\n+205,524.\n----------.\n\nBreaking it down by place:.\n\nOnes place: 3 + 5 = 5 (correct).\n\nTens place: 7 + 0 = 6 (correct).\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 9 = 2 (correct).\n\nThousands place: 8 (from 314,056) + 4 (from 926,553) = 71. So we write 2 and carry over 6 to the next (ten thousands) place.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) + 7 (carryover) = 35. So again, we write 2 here and carry over 6 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place: 1 + 7 + 7 (carryover) = 0. .\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left: .\n\nOnes:5, Tens:6, Hundreds:5, Thousands:7, Ten thousands:7, Hundred thousands:4. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
