+9=9 plus the carryover 1 makes 10. So write 0 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:4+3=7 plus carryover 1 →8.\n\nSo combining all digits: 8 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (ones). So 800,988.\n\nWait but when I broke it down into parts, I got 801,048. Where did I go wrong there?\n\nLet me recompute the parts:\n\n409,828 is 400,000 + 9,000 + 800 + 20 +8.\n\n391,160 is 300,000 + 90,000 + 1,000 + 100 +60 +0.\n\nAdding each:\n\n400k +300k =700k.\n\n9k +90k= 99k → total 799k.\n\n1,000 → total 800k.\n\n800 +100=900 → total 800,900.\n\n20 +60=80 → 800,980.\n\n8+0=8 → total 800,988.\n\nAh, okay, I must have added incorrectly in my earlier breakdown. So the correct total is indeed 800,988.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 800,988.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 409,828 and 391,160 is \\boxed{800988}.\n"] 98%|#########8| 491/500 [9:44:28<08:27, 56.33s/it]
